        {
          "id": 709427645,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "If you see the original patches from osmo-pcu.git we basically use both fExist and isnull, since they are actually expressing different things:we use fExist to print whether the \"Exist\" bit was 1 or 0, and isnull whether there is actually something to keep decoding in \"next\" items.\nIn wireshark's case, since there's no use of fExist, because it is taken directly from the tvb, it had to be removed (compiler errors).\nThe logic for the checks above I think are far easy to understand/follow by using \"isnull\" instead, that's also why. If you still want me to reimplement it using fExist (as in negation of isnull, not as in if \"Exist\" bit is 1), then say so, but I'd personally prefer keeping it this way.",
          "author": {
            "id": 3212477,
            "username": "pespin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "pespin.shar@gmail.com",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2bdd79a151c775a34e767cdef6cd400c152bee8db77654b502f00ef7a7dd758c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pespin"
